==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|bulla||bubble|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|bullae}}

# {{medicine}} A [[blister]], [[vesicle]], or other thin-walled cavity or [[lesion]].
# {{archaeology}} A clay envelope or hollow ball, typ. with seal impressions or writing on its outside indicating its contents.
# {{historical}} In ancient Rome, a kind of [[amulet]] or [[boss]].
# Later, handwritten document from the papal chancellery.

